{"content":{"attachment":{"filename":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq/TODOS.md","snippet":"1\t# TODO\n2\t\n3\tRemaining work, organized by area. All completed items stripped.\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## Paper — cluster-reliant items (filed 2026-08-23)\n8\t\n9\tEverything here needs `/fss-data` (run dirs, artifacts, or GPUs). The paper's prose is\n10\twritten against these being resolved; each maps to a `\\fillin{}` / LaTeX comment in\n11\t`paper/sections/`. Run `python scripts/check_grounding.py` after any of them.\n12\t\n13\t### Audit the wiki community_pack negative (suspected corruption) — BLOCKS §7 wiki paragraph\n14\t`RESULTS_graph_sparsity.md` §4 / `docs/handoff_wiki_crossdoc.md` report solo-wiki\n15\tcross-doc Δnll on `val_community` as small but consistently NEGATIVE (−0.02, tight CIs),\n16\twhile HotpotQA-cross-doc on the same ckpts is +1.29. Human suspects the community_pack\n17\tfinding is a harness/corruption artifact, not real. Re-derive from scratch: (a) rebuild\n18\tthe wiki_merged val_community packs and confirm grants are the RIGHT edges (not stale\n19\tschedule/normalization drift — see the \"schedule staleness\" memory); (b) check the\n20\tOption-B `span.start+1` grant keying and the `max_seq_len` 2048-default bug do not apply;\n21\t(c) score the identical packs with the HotpotQA-style paired scorer as a cross-check;\n22\t(d) widen to seeds 0–2 / 500 packs. Until resolved the paper makes NO claim about\n23\tgeneric held-out wiki text (§7 \"The Wikipedia community-pack measurement\"). If it is\n24\treal, the fit-dependence hypothesis in the handoff becomes an appendix result.\n25\t\n26\t### arXiv is scoped OUT until sequence-parallel training exists\n27\tarXiv papers are long relative to the 32k window, so packs hold 1–2 docs, targets are\n28\trarely co-packed, and the cross-doc mask has ~nothing to grant (sparsity eff.\n29\tgrants/pack = 1.5, Δ flat). The arXiv sweep (cdl val 2.471 vs dc 2.156) is therefore\n30\tuninformative about the method. §4 states this; no arXiv claim is made. Re-enable only\n31\tafter implementing sequence-parallel / context-parallel training (ring/striped attention\n32\tover the BIM kernels) so a citation neighbourhood fits in one logical sequence. Also\n33\tnote the `\\cite`-in-`%`-comment detector gap (App. C) before re-running.\n34\t\n35\t### Measure the actual thesis: native corpus-fetching generation from pretraining alone\n36\tThe design's purpose (§1, §7, §8) is that `cross_doc_link` teaches, via plain NTP under\n37\tmaintained causality, that EMITTING a reference is what opens access to the referenced\n38\tdoc — so a trained model can fetch from its corpus by generating a citation, with no\n39\tretriever/fusion/SFT/RL. This is UNMEASURED. The density result (dc-trained model gets\n40\tnearly the full cross-doc benefit at eval) is about *reading* a handed target, not\n41\t*asking* for one, and must not stand in for it. Design a measurement that works at\n42\t~350M params where free generation is incoherent. Candidates:\n43\t- **Link-emission rate under teacher forcing**: at positions where the reference doc\n44\t  contains a link, compare P(link-opener) and P(correct target title | opener) for cdl vs\n45\t  dc vs concat_link models. Cheap, no free generation, uses existing annotator openers.\n46\t- **Constrained-decoding resolution rate**: force the opener, decode the target with the\n47\t  trie/title index, measure fraction resolving to a corpus doc and to the RIGHT doc.\n48\t- **Counterfactual use**: after a resolved fetch, Δnll of the continuation with the\n49\t  fetched doc vs a deranged doc (placebo) — does the model USE what it asked for?\n50\t- **Scale ladder**: the honest test needs a model that generates coherently; plan the\n51\t  first size at which free-generation link-following becomes measurable.\n52\tFold into the eval harness as a first-class benchmark; report cdl vs dc vs concat_link.\n53\t\n54\t### HotpotQA / RepoBench headline placebo (TENTATIVE — may already be done)\n55\tHuman believes the derangement placebo for the headline arms (`TODOS` \"Placebo/\n56\tderangement on the headline arms\", filed 08-10) may have been implemented in a local\n57\tworktree on fss (`/fss/evin_t/tagseq2tagseq-*`) and NOT pushed. Check `git -C\n58\t/fss/evin_t/tagseq2tagseq* status` / unpushed branches before re-implementing. Once\n59\tlanded: run on the wiki bfs headline ckpt + Java/Python RepoBench arms, add ledger keys\n60\t`crossdoc.wiki_hotpotqa.placebo_sep` etc., cite in §6.1 / §7 Limitations.\n61\t\n62\t### Wiki concat-control HotpotQA eval (missing) — `\\fillin` in §6.3\n63\t`wiki_docconcatlink_best` (run_20260717_234605_156456, wd0.3, best_model.pt) has\n64\tsingle-doc evals but NO `hotpotqa_cross_doc` eval in any record; `wiki_docconcat_best`\n65\t(run_20260717_234603_647704) has no eval at all. Run `hotpotqa_cross_doc` on the\n66\tconcat_link ckpt (mask has links, so the cross arm is well-defined) and the single-doc\n67\tpanel + held-out ppl on the concat ckpt; distill; add `compute.wiki_hotpotqa.*` keys.\n68\tThen §6.3's \"matching contrast on Wikipedia\" and Table Z.3 get a `doc_concatenated`\n69\tcolumn.\n70\t\n71\t### Provenance: `kind: log` source for the two val-loss literals\n72\t`traversal.wiki_val_loss.{graph,random}` are literals. Implement a `log` source in\n73\t`scripts/provenance_lib.py` that parses `runs/<id>/logs/metrics_rank_0.jsonl`\n74\t(`val_loss_mean`, last/min row) and have `distill_runs.py` snapshot the needed rows into\n75\tthe record so it survives run-dir deletion. Same source unlocks the LR/WD U-curve tables\n76\tand the per-language sweep val-loss table for App. Z.\n77\t\n78\t### Provenance: `kind: artifact` source for the sparsity-scaling JSONs — BLOCKS §6.5 numbers\n79\t§6.5 (link-density dose–response) is written with `\\fillin` magnitudes; the values are\n80\tin `/fss-data/evin_t/tagseq2tagseq_artifacts/sparsity_scaling/{phase1_eval,\n81\tphase2_traintime,grid2d,effective_density.json,regression.json}` and listed in a LaTeX\n82\tcomment under §6.5. Add an `artifact` source (path + JSON pointer, content-hashed, copied\n83\tinto `provenance/artifacts/`) and ground: eval-time code-only r/slope/intercept/n,\n84\ttrain-time r, out-degree r, per-dataset Δ@κ=1 + eff. grants/pack, 2D-grid axis swings,\n85\tkeep0-row TS dc-trained vs cdl-trained. Also copy `fig_sparsity.png`, `fig_traintime.png`,\n86\t`fig_grid2d.png`, `regression.png` into `paper/figures/` and wire them into §6.5. Finish\n87\tthe full 6-dataset keep0 row (SLURM 81104) and the traversal-time TS spot-check (81106–08)\n88\tfirst so the section reports final numbers.\n89\t\n90\t### Density-aware timing: locate the originating run — `\\fillin` in §6.7\n91\tThe 1.45×/1.14× speedup and CoV numbers in README.md come from `step_timing_rank*.csv`\n92\tfiles that are not in-repo and carry no run_id (2 nodes × 2 GPUs, The Stack 10M, 32k).\n93\tFind the run on `/fss-data` (or re-time: one live vs one precomputed short run at the\n94\tsame world_size/node layout), archive the CSVs under `provenance/artifacts/`, ground via\n95\tthe `artifact` source above.\n96\t\n97\t### Diversity section — blocked on the corrected merged_v2 re-run\n98\t§6.6 is fully `\\fillin`. All `merged_all_v2` models were retracted 2026-08-14\n99\t(sequential-not-interleaved loader). Re-run at 3.9B/8B/16B (corrected LR from the 16B\n100\tsweep) with all four masks (configs `merged_v2_*`), then ports (use_line, Tier-2 placebo)\n101\t+ specialist re-pull for an exact table, distill, ground. Note in the paper: rungs are\n102\tindependent samples, not nested; packs are within-source (multi-task mixing, not\n103\tcross-source attention).\n104\t\n105\t### Dataset table cells — `\\fillin` in §4 Table 1\n106\tMissing: wiki_merged edges + mean out-degree (+ token count: RESULTS says 4 epochs ≈\n107\t3.8B tok); JS / Dart / Zig edge counts + out-degree; Go / Java out-degree; arXiv\n108\tnodes/edges (README says 2.20M nodes ~10B tok; framing notes say ~1.98M — reconcile).\n109\tRead each dataset's `metadata.json` / audit log under\n110\t`/fss-data/evin_t/tagseq2tagseq_artifacts/pretokenized_datasets/<ds>/`.\n111\t\n112\t### Link-reliance probe: synthetic cross-doc versions of standard benchmarks (filed 2026-08-26)\n113\tHow heavily does the model actually rely on the links it references? Build\n114\tcross-doc-link versions of regular, non-HotpotQA-like benchmarks (e.g. HellaSwag):\n115\tinject a synthetic link into the question body and score the completion with an aux doc\n\n... [623 lines truncated] ...","type":"edited_text_file"},"injection_type":"attachment/edited_text_file"},"context":{"branch":"paper-prose-draft","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq","head":"66ae5bc942464f47e6398e0ac64d929a2aa9663f","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/tagseq2tagseq.git"},"id":"ev2-9994555d371f63e15214ae1790e15056fd435014685e233c10dc2840ebc93085","kind":"context_injection","meta":{"actor":{"type":"system"},"session_id":"5cbbe416-90e8-4a21-93e7-044acf862880","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.252"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-01T17:15:11.635Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"attachment":{"filename":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq/TODOS.md","snippet":"1\t# TODO\n2\t\n3\tRemaining work, organized by area. All completed items stripped.\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## Paper — cluster-reliant items (filed 2026-08-23)\n8\t\n9\tEverything here needs `/fss-data` (run dirs, artifacts, or GPUs). The paper's prose is\n10\twritten against these being resolved; each maps to a `\\fillin{}` / LaTeX comment in\n11\t`paper/sections/`. Run `python scripts/check_grounding.py` after any of them.\n12\t\n13\t### Audit the wiki community_pack negative (suspected corruption) — BLOCKS §7 wiki paragraph\n14\t`RESULTS_graph_sparsity.md` §4 / `docs/handoff_wiki_crossdoc.md` report solo-wiki\n15\tcross-doc Δnll on `val_community` as small but consistently NEGATIVE (−0.02,